{"name":"Almost Plum","hex":"#beb0c2","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very close to, but not quite.","Up to, except for a negligible set (where negligible is not universally but contextually defined)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something or someone that doesn't quite make it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almost"},{"term":"plum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit and its tree.","Extended senses."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark bluish-red colour.","Choice; especially lavish or preferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almost","blocks":[{"text":"In set theory, when dealing with sets of infinite size, the term almost or nearly is used to refer to all but a negligible amount of elements in the set. The notion of \"negligible\" depends on the context, and may mean \"of measure zero\", \"finite\", or \"countable\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almost","wikidata":"Q840148"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)","wikidata":"Q3108